{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791592333,"nonce":"LMxED39FwNiQstI8eY1+SB+WRvs=","title":"Python inference spells names on every lookup","message":"Inference runs each body many times (go: five infer_module calls of four inner rounds each), so per-lookup costs multiply. A go start-up profile (ZYPY_PROFILE_STARTUP=300, Apple M-series) had 637 of 11599 samples in fmt::format_inner, mostly from:\n\n- Module::method_sig formatting \"Class$method\" to look the method's function up (366 samples inclusive);\n- Typer/Lowerer::module_member_of formatting the dotted path of every attribute chain, also for chains rooted at a local such as self.x.y (288);\n- Module::denest formatting the field's \"$lists\" key even when no field is dynamic (101).\n\nlist_sites also typed the receiver of every attribute call to look for followed fields when no followed field had that attribute's name, and typed a method call's receiver twice; overriders scanned every class rather than the owner's descendants.\n\nStart-up instructions, run stopped once start-up is done (an unknown option to the kernel), ZYPY_PROFILE_STARTUP=10, median of 3, same build features (llvm-backend, LLVM off at run time):\n\n  total of 22 kernels 155.75G -\u003e 152.16G (-2.3%)\n  go -5.0%, richards -5.8%, pyflate -5.3%, deltablue -4.6%, hexiom2 -3.2%, scimark_* -1.6 to -3.2%\n  nqueens varies by +-8% between runs of the same binary; its result is noise.\n\n22 of 22 speed-kernel checksums equal CPython's.","files":null}]}